  "conclusions": [
    "Kernel execution occupies about 90-91% of the latest capture windows; matrix multiplication is about 85% of summed kernel durations.",
    "The current main matrix path is quantized MMQ, not uniformly FP16.",
    "H2D coverage is concurrent activity, not a counterfactual critical-path saving or SM utilization.",
    "Higher coverage was measured, but a material end-to-end speedup was not established; keep both experimental flags off by default.",
    "Unchanged projections and attention also slowed in the combined capture. Resource contention, run-condition drift and merged-kernel scheduling have not been isolated.",
    "With transfer bytes/rate fixed, compute and communication activity become comparable after roughly 8-9x kernel acceleration; local dependencies and host staging can limit earlier.",
    "The approximate 1100 tokens/s H2D-only ceiling uses the current payload and observed activity rate, not a portable GPU upper bound."
  ]
